    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a 2022 F-150 in the shop. Customer is complaining about the transmission slipping under load. I've got the scan tool hooked up and I'm seeing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. What are the most likely things causing these kinds of pressure fluctuations in a modern automatic like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit may be caused by a faulty or premature seat drive failure, clogged or dirty solenoid filters, or inadequate seal set pressure. In a modern automatic like the 2022 F-150, the transmission may also have a hydraulic capacity transposition logic error or an electronic control unit (ECU) malfunction. Furthermore, excessive transmission fluid contamination or improper flushing could also lead to these issues. Check the transmission fluid level, condition, and test the solenoids for proper operation.",
      "source": "target",
